Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 14 05:22:42 2026 +0000

    fix: purge forbidden /ships.html links site-wide + CI regression guard (issue #1708)
    
    The seven generators named in #1708 were verified already fixed in-tree
    (all emit /ships/). The live content they'd polluted was not: 797 files
    still carried the forbidden hub link. Fixed in three counted passes:
    
    - href="/ships.html" → href="/ships/": 669 replacements (nav pills,
      body links) incl. assets/js/ship-port-links.js allShipsUrl (15 lines,
      the shared runtime component) — external booking URLs (Costa,
      Silversea, HAL) untouched by construction (patterns anchored to
      internal forms).
    - JSON-LD/absolute "https://cruisinginthewake.com/ships.html[#carnival]"
      → /ships/: 329 replacements (BreadcrumbList items; #carnival resolves
      nowhere, breadcrumbs point at the canonical hub — ships.html's own
      rel=canonical already declares /ships/).
    - Emitted ai-breadcrumbs 'parent: /ships.html' in
      data/atlas/generate-ship-stubs.js: 1.
    
    NEW CI job 'Forbidden Ships Link Guard' in quality.yml fails on all
    three fixed forms. Probed live: exit 0 on clean tree, exit 1 on an
    injected violation, exit 0 after cleanup; YAML parses.
    
    DEFERRED LOUDLY (not silently): 221 href="/ships.html#<class>" deep
    links remain — those anchors resolve only on the legacy ships.html page
    today (oasis/voyager/vision/radiance/freedom/quantum) or nowhere
    (#carnival, #excel-class); rewriting them to /ships/ would break 214
    working deep-links. Registered as HLS itw-ships-html-fragment-links
    (P2) with the anchor inventory; the guard's fragment exclusion is
    documented in the workflow comment.
    
    sw.js isShipsIndexPage legacy detector left as-is (dead code, detects
    inbound legacy URLs, emits nothing).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
